Targeted Advice:
Include Order: Ensure that memory/types.h is included before any header or source file that uses sep::memory::MemoryTierEnum. Review the include directives in the affected files and reorder them if necessary. Standard library headers should generally come first, followed by project-specific headers, ensuring dependencies are included before the code that uses them.
Forward Declarations: While you have struct SEPBlenderBridge; in compat/component_bridge.h, you need the full definition of MemoryTierEnum wherever it's being used directly (e.g., as a type for a member variable or function parameter). Forward declarations are not sufficient in these cases.
Namespace: Double-check that MemoryTierEnum is correctly defined within the sep::memory namespace in memory/types.h. And when referencing it outside the sep::memory namespace, use the fully qualified name sep::memory::MemoryTierEnum.
